{
  "version": "sketch/1",
  "title": "Converge, Fork, Return",
  "caption": "The essay funnels a wide worry about conscious AI into three psychological biases that converge on 'it's pareidolia,' then into four independent arguments that converge on 'functionalism is shaky,' then forks into two distinct ethical risks, before looping back to its opening warning that mistaking machines for us means underestimating ourselves.",
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "overview",
      "title": "Overview: temptation, argument, ethics, loop",
      "height": 1200,
      "items": [
        {
          "kind": "node",
          "id": "opening",
          "shape": "ellipse",
          "x": 280,
          "y": 40,
          "w": 200,
          "h": 70,
          "text": "Could AI really be conscious?",
          "size": "md",
          "sub": "and why it would matter",
          "detail": "Consciousness brings moral status; getting this wrong distorts ethics either way.",
          "block": "spya-e68t9h"
        },
        {
          "kind": "region",
          "x": 20,
          "y": 130,
          "w": 720,
          "h": 240,
          "style": "band",
          "label": "WHY WE'RE TEMPTED TO SEE IT",
          "tone": 1
        },
        {
          "kind": "node",
          "id": "bias1",
          "shape": "box",
          "x": 40,
          "y": 170,
          "w": 200,
          "h": 80,
          "text": "Anthropocentrism & exceptionalism",
          "size": "sm",
          "sub": "human traits as the template",
          "detail": "Three overlapping biases make us see human qualities as definitional.",
          "tone": 1,
          "block": "spya-cvaqgs"
        },
        {
          "kind": "node",
          "id": "bias2",
          "shape": "box",
          "x": 280,
          "y": 170,
          "w": 200,
          "h": 80,
          "text": "Fluent language reads as feeling",
          "size": "sm",
          "sub": "'hallucinate' vs 'confabulate'",
          "detail": "LLMs pull our strings via language; AlphaFold doesn't, though it's similar under the hood.",
          "tone": 1,
          "block": "spya-k6fpme"
        },
        {
          "kind": "node",
          "id": "bias3",
          "shape": "box",
          "x": 520,
          "y": 170,
          "w": 200,
          "h": 80,
          "text": "Exponential hype & techno-rapture",
          "size": "sm",
          "sub": "every point feels like a threshold",
          "detail": "Exponential curves and dreams of digital immortality inflate expectations.",
          "tone": 1,
          "block": "spya-cke6sj"
        },
        {
          "kind": "node",
          "id": "hub_pareidolia",
          "shape": "hex",
          "x": 240,
          "y": 280,
          "w": 280,
          "h": 70,
          "text": "Mostly pareidolia — but that's only step one",
          "size": "md",
          "detail": "Recognizing the bias doesn't settle whether real artificial consciousness is possible.",
          "tone": 1,
          "block": "spya-k850tu"
        },
        {
          "kind": "node",
          "id": "comp_assumption",
          "shape": "diamond",
          "x": 280,
          "y": 395,
          "w": 200,
          "h": 65,
          "text": "Assumes: computation = consciousness",
          "size": "sm",
          "sub": "computational functionalism",
          "detail": "The whole case for conscious AI rests on this usually-unexamined assumption.",
          "block": "spya-d3g67c"
        },
        {
          "kind": "region",
          "x": 20,
          "y": 485,
          "w": 720,
          "h": 270,
          "style": "band",
          "label": "FOUR ARGUMENTS AGAINST THAT ASSUMPTION",
          "tone": 2
        },
        {
          "kind": "node",
          "id": "arg1",
          "shape": "box",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 525,
          "w": 155,
          "h": 95,
          "text": "Brains aren't software on hardware",
          "size": "xs",
          "detail": "No clean separation of mindware and wetware exists in real brains.",
          "tone": 2,
          "block": "spya-sk4su6"
        },
        {
          "kind": "node",
          "id": "arg2",
          "shape": "box",
          "x": 205,
          "y": 525,
          "w": 155,
          "h": 95,
          "text": "Other dynamics beyond Turing computation",
          "size": "xs",
          "detail": "Continuous, analogue, and dynamical processes may matter more than algorithms.",
          "tone": 2,
          "block": "spya-affgsh"
        },
        {
          "kind": "node",
          "id": "arg3",
          "shape": "box",
          "x": 380,
          "y": 525,
          "w": 155,
          "h": 95,
          "text": "Life itself may be necessary",
          "size": "xs",
          "detail": "Consciousness may be tied to self-sustaining, living, predictive bodies.",
          "tone": 2,
          "block": "spya-e7jqx4"
        },
        {
          "kind": "node",
          "id": "arg4",
          "shape": "box",
          "x": 555,
          "y": 525,
          "w": 155,
          "h": 95,
          "text": "Simulating a mind ≠ creating one",
          "size": "xs",
          "detail": "A simulated storm doesn't get anything wet; mind-uploading assumes its conclusion.",
          "tone": 2,
          "block": "spya-cqh5wq"
        },
        {
          "kind": "node",
          "id": "summary_hub",
          "shape": "hex",
          "x": 240,
          "y": 650,
          "w": 280,
          "h": 75,
          "text": "Functionalism looks shaky, not impossible",
          "size": "md",
          "detail": "Each argument stands alone but together they weaken the case for conscious AI.",
          "tone": 2,
          "block": "spya-uzr60x"
        },
        {
          "kind": "node",
          "id": "ethics_uncertainty",
          "shape": "diamond",
          "x": 280,
          "y": 790,
          "w": 200,
          "h": 65,
          "text": "Given the uncertainty, don't build it",
          "size": "sm",
          "detail": "Deliberately creating conscious AI would risk new, uncontrollable suffering.",
          "block": "spya-e7fdmb"
        },
        {
          "kind": "region",
          "x": 20,
          "y": 880,
          "w": 720,
          "h": 150,
          "style": "band",
          "label": "TWO DISTINCT RISKS",
          "tone": 3
        },
        {
          "kind": "node",
          "id": "real_risk",
          "shape": "box",
          "x": 80,
          "y": 920,
          "w": 260,
          "h": 85,
          "text": "If AI really is conscious: disaster",
          "size": "sm",
          "sub": "new suffering, hard to switch off",
          "detail": "Rights would make dangerous systems harder to control or shut down.",
          "tone": 3,
          "block": "spya-vs0vpj"
        },
        {
          "kind": "node",
          "id": "seeming_risk",
          "shape": "box",
          "x": 420,
          "y": 920,
          "w": 260,
          "h": 85,
          "text": "If it only seems conscious: illusion persists",
          "size": "sm",
          "sub": "no test can settle it",
          "detail": "Like a visual illusion, the feeling of AI consciousness survives knowing better.",
          "tone": 3,
          "block": "spya-gwz5eu"
        },
        {
          "kind": "node",
          "id": "closing",
          "shape": "ellipse",
          "x": 240,
          "y": 1070,
          "w": 280,
          "h": 90,
          "text": "Recover a soul that's more breath than machine",
          "size": "md",
          "sub": "embodied, not disembodied rationality",
          "detail": "Mistaking algorithms for minds means overestimating them and underestimating ourselves.",
          "block": "spya-zv36xq"
        },
