    {
      "id": "inside-computation",
      "title": "Inside: four arguments against functionalism",
      "height": 500,
      "items": [
        {
          "kind": "node",
          "id": "c_intro",
          "shape": "ellipse",
          "x": 280,
          "y": 40,
          "w": 200,
          "h": 60,
          "text": "Assumption: computation suffices",
          "size": "md",
          "detail": "Computational functionalism, so ingrained it's rarely recognized as an assumption.",
          "block": "spya-wepmnr"
        },
        {
          "kind": "node",
          "id": "c1a",
          "shape": "box",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 150,
          "w": 150,
          "h": 80,
          "text": "Turing: software is hardware-independent",
          "size": "xs",
          "detail": "A universal Turing machine can run any algorithm on any suitable substrate.",
          "block": "spya-cf70dt"
        },
        {
          "kind": "node",
          "id": "c1b",
          "shape": "box",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 260,
          "w": 150,
          "h": 80,
          "text": "But brains have no such split",
          "size": "xs",
          "detail": "What a brain does and what it is cannot be cleanly separated.",
          "block": "spya-b0086e"
        },
        {
          "kind": "node",
          "id": "c2a",
          "shape": "box",
          "x": 215,
          "y": 150,
          "w": 150,
          "h": 80,
          "text": "Continuous, stochastic dynamics exceed algorithms",
          "size": "xs",
          "detail": "Electromagnetic fields, neurotransmitter flux — none strictly Turing-computable.",
          "block": "spya-n393ru"
        },
        {
          "kind": "node",
          "id": "c2b",
          "shape": "box",
          "x": 215,
          "y": 260,
          "w": 150,
          "h": 80,
          "text": "Watt's governor: regulation, not computation",
          "size": "xs",
          "detail": "A 'computational' version of the governor would misunderstand what's going on.",
          "block": "spya-sq9v5k"
        },
        {
          "kind": "node",
          "id": "c3a",
          "shape": "box",
          "x": 400,
          "y": 150,
          "w": 150,
          "h": 80,
          "text": "Perception as controlled hallucination",
          "size": "xs",
          "detail": "Conscious experience as the brain's best guess, calibrated by sensory signals.",
          "block": "spya-xhvztm"
        },
        {
          "kind": "node",
          "id": "c3b",
          "shape": "box",
          "x": 400,
          "y": 260,
          "w": 150,
          "h": 80,
          "text": "Self-sustaining life grounds prediction",
          "size": "xs",
          "detail": "Prediction-error minimization is inseparable from the materiality of metabolism.",
          "block": "spya-vys3vj"
        },
        {
          "kind": "node",
          "id": "c4a",
          "shape": "box",
          "x": 585,
          "y": 150,
          "w": 150,
          "h": 80,
          "text": "A simulated storm doesn't get you wet",
          "size": "xs",
          "detail": "Simulation lacks the causal powers of the thing simulated.",
          "block": "spya-npjt4j"
        },
        {
          "kind": "node",
          "id": "c4b",
          "shape": "box",
          "x": 585,
          "y": 260,
          "w": 150,
          "h": 80,
          "text": "Mind-uploading assumes its own conclusion",
          "size": "xs",
          "detail": "You're no more likely to exist in the sim than a hailstorm is to arise in a weather computer.",
          "block": "spya-xvm37k"
        },
        {
          "kind": "node",
          "id": "c_hub",
          "shape": "hex",
          "x": 240,
          "y": 380,
          "w": 280,
          "h": 80,
          "text": "A strong, shaky assumption",
          "size": "md",
          "detail": "Four independent lines each weaken computational functionalism, and together they compound.",
          "block": "spya-uzr60x"
        },
        {
          "kind": "edge",
